        "counter corruption": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright speaks for the wizards, and he takes the cult very seriously\u2014pushing for aggressive magical detection and containment measures.\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright is the council\u2019s arcane representative. As Head of the Wizard\u2019s College, he advocates a proactive, magic-heavy response to the cult threat.\n\nHis angle on the cult is clear and consistent:\n- He views the corrupted meat as a perversion of magic (CANON).\n- He is deeply troubled by the dark magic involved (CANON).\n- He plans to deploy magical solutions, including a rune to detect corruption and potentially a full magical lockdown of the city (OBSERVED).\n- He is eager to mobilize the Wizard\u2019s College\u2019s resources to detect and counteract the cult\u2019s influence (OBSERVED).\n\nThere are no conflicting facts about his stance\u2014both CANON and OBSERVED align that he is strongly anti-cult and favors decisive arcane intervention.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Head of the Wizard\u2019s College; council representative for arcane interests\n- Goals: Magical lockdown; detection rune; deploy arcane resources\n- Alignment toward cult: Views it as dangerous, corrupting magic that must be stopped\n- Approach: Investigative and preventative through large-scale spellwork",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
