        "killing blow": "hit",
        "bonogo": "hit",
        "decapitated": "hit"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight **dead**\u2014specifically **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**\u2014with Bonogo taking the head.\n\nThere are conflicting OBSERVED states for **the Wolf**: earlier in the fight he **\u201cDisappeared (became invisible)\u201d** and was **\u201cAttempting to escape through a secret passage while invisible.\u201d** However, a later OBSERVED outcome tied to **ent_bonogo** resolves this: Bonogo **\u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it,\u201d** and the Wolf\u2019s physical condition explicitly includes **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d**\n\nBecause decapitation is a terminal outcome and is recorded as a completed event, it overrides the earlier escape attempt. So the final, current state is that the Wolf did not get away\u2014he was killed in the chamber (or immediately after pursuit) and is now a corpse missing its head.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Status: **Dead (Decapitated; head removed from body)**\n- Final handler: **ent_bonogo (took the head)**\n- Prior state (superseded): Invisible, fleeing via secret passage",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
