      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The chamber actively interferes via **activated runes/arcane wards, illusory walls, trap bursts (damage + paralysis), and environmental hazards like debris and verticality**, often targeting anyone without council amulets.\n\nThe **Council Chambers** themselves are a hazard engine:\n\n- **Arcane wards & runes (OBSERVED):** \u201crunes along the walls activated when Caelynn cast her spell\u201d \u2014 these trigger defensive effects mid-fight, including **arcane trap bursts** that can deal **2d6 force damage** and **temporarily paralyze** (tied to Players\u2019 physical_condition).\n- **Targeting logic (CANON):** Council members have amulets marking them as friendly, so **traps may target the players** if they lack them.\n- **Illusory walls (OBSERVED):** Portions of the room are false, causing **disorientation and movement disruption** (Players already noted as disoriented by illusion effects).\n- **Falling debris (OBSERVED):** The fight destabilizes the space, forcing players to **dodge falling debris hazards**.\n- **Vertical problem (OBSERVED):** **High, arched ceilings** make enemies at elevation hard to reach (e.g., \u201cUnable to reach Karsemine due to height\u201d).\n- **Hidden trapdoor (OBSERVED):** \u0905\u091a\u093e\u0928\u0915 repositioning or ambush vector.\n- **Spell volatility (OBSERVED):** \u201calmost the entire room is lit up by Fireball\u201d \u2014 spells escalate unpredictably in the confined, warded space.\n- **Audio/pressure cues (CANON/OBSERVED):** The room\u2019s acoustics and the **hum shifting** can signal triggers or incoming reinforcements.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Geography: Large circular room, central table, high ceilings, hidden trapdoor\n- Defenses: Ancient wards, activated runes, illusory walls, trap bursts\n- Atmosphere: Fireball-lit chaos, thick anticipation, sound carries\n- Physical Condition: Disheveled, shedding debris",
