      "answer": "TL;DR: Delay gives the cult time to act\u2014using hidden routes and possible council influence\u2014to complete the summoning and sabotage the city from within, pushing the city closer to disaster.\n\nIf the council stalls, the biggest threat is momentum shifting to **the cult**.  \n- CANON + OBSERVED: The cult is already active beneath the city, using **hidden routes** and infrastructure (sewers, passages) to move and operate undetected.  \n- CANON: Their goals include **accessing the heart of the city**, **corrupting cauldrons**, and **completing a summoning (flesh kaiju)**.  \n- CANON: They also have **influence in the council**, meaning inaction may not be neutral\u2014it may be exactly what some factions want.\n\nMeanwhile, the city is already **\u201cbrought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate.\u201d** (OBSERVED). A delayed response risks:  \n- Coordinated attacks across the city landing unopposed (CANON geography)  \n- Weak points in defenses being exploited (CANON defenses)  \n- A failed or mistimed **planned magical lockdown**, potentially isolating districts or trapping civilians (OBSERVED)\n\nIn short: talking buys the cult time, and time is exactly what their plan requires.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Governance: Council deadlock; cult influence in council (OBSERVED + CANON)  \n- Threat: Cult summoning, sabotage, hidden movement (CANON)  \n- City Status: \u201cbrought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate\u201d (OBSERVED)  \n- Defenses: Known weak points; lockdown plan not yet executed (CANON + OBSERVED)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
