      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead at the end of Session 12\u2014he was **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** His prior corruption (e.g., **\u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d**) is no longer an active state due to death.\n\nThe OBSERVED facts include multiple states (invisible, escaping, damaged), but the terminal outcome overrides them: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** This is reinforced by Bonogo\u2019s role note: he **\u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it.\u201d** Per the terminal outcome rule, this is the final and current state.\n\nBefore death, the Wolf clearly showed signs of corruption (e.g., **\u201cWolf has an oily sheen to his eyes.\u201d**) and erratic mental state (begging to be killed, regret), suggesting he was still under influence. However, no OBSERVED fact indicates that corruption was cleansed prior to death.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Physical Condition (OBSERVED): **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d**, previously invisible and heavily damaged  \n- Mental State (OBSERVED): desperate, regretful, begging for release  \n- Alignment/Context (OBSERVED): cult-affiliated, corrupted influence present  \n- Operational Status (OBSERVED): attempting escape prior to death  \n\nConclusion: Dead, formerly corrupted; no evidence of purification before death.",
