      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive cult saboteur manipulating events and trying to escape; after, he is **Decapitated; head removed from body**, ending his agency and shifting him from manipulator to evidence.\n\nBefore (pre-/during fight):\n- OBSERVED: The Wolf is a **second-in-command** guard and **cultist** working to **sabotage council decision-making** and mislead via Deception.\n- CANON: Uses **illusory duplicates** and confusion tactics.\n- OBSERVED: Actively **attempting escape** (Invisibility potion, secret tunnel) and **ordering allies (Thalia) to attack**.\n- OBSERVED: Mentally **desperate**, \u201cbegging\u2026to be killed,\u201d suggesting internal conflict or corruption.\n- OBSERVED: Physically **mobile, invisible at times**, and taking damage but still acting.\n\nAfter (post-fight outcome):\n- OBSERVED (terminal): **Decapitated; head removed from body**.\n- OBSERVED: No longer operational\u2014escape, deception, and combat all cease.\n- OBSERVED: His body (notably with **oily sheen to his eyes**) becomes a **source of information** (players plan Speak with Dead).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Enemy saboteur \u2192 Corpse/evidence\n- Operational Status: Escaping/manipulating \u2192 Neutralized\n- Mental State: Desperate/conflicted \u2192 N/A (dead)\n- Physical Condition: Invisible/damaged \u2192 **Decapitated; head removed from body**\n- Narrative Function: Active antagonist \u2192 Clue-bearing aftermath object",
